    "text": "© 2026 SaturdayDownSouth.com Home > News > Sports > How to Watch Tennessee Volunteers vs Virginia: TV Channel, Tip-Off Time & Postseason Info Ad Disclosure This article/post contains references to products or services from one or more of our advertisers or partners. We may receive compensation when you click on links to those products or services. The No. 3 seed Virginia Cavaliers take on the No. 6 seed Tennessee Volunteers in a Round of 32 matchup in the 2026 NCAA Men’s Basketball Postseason. Virginia enters the game with a 30-5 record after defeating Wright State. This marks their first tournament win since 2019 under new head coach Ryan Odom. Meanwhile, Rick Barnes and his Tennessee squad bring a 23-11 record following a first-round victory over Miami (Ohio). Watch Tennesseee vs Virginia on Sling TV. The winner of this neutral-site game advances to the Sweet 16 to face either Iowa State or Kentucky. The matchup tests Virginia’s disciplined Atlantic Coast Conference pedigree against Tennessee’s Southeastern Conference rebounding attack. For fans looking to follow the action live, read on to find everything you need to know about the game, including the official tip-off time, location details, TV channel and available streaming options. When is Tennessee vs Virginia? What Time Does it Start? The postseason matchup between the Tennessee Volunteers and the Virginia Cavaliers is scheduled for March 22, 2026. Tip-off is set for 6:10 PM ET. The neutral-site game will be played at Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Where is Tennessee vs Virginia? The upcoming game takes place at Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. While the event is being played at a neutral site, the Virginia Cavaliers serve as the designated home team. The Tennessee Volunteers are the designated away team for the matchup. How Can I Watch Tennessee vs Virginia? Fans looking to tune in to the postseason matchup between the Tennessee Volunteers and the Virginia Cavaliers can watch the game live on television on TNT. TNT serves as the exclusive television network broadcasting the event. The network provides full coverage of the neutral-site contest starting at the scheduled 6:10 PM ET tip-off. How Can I Stream Tennessee vs Virginia? With the broadcast rights belonging to TNT, fans have multiple digital options to stream the postseason matchup. Viewers with a traditional cable or satellite subscription can stream the game directly through the TNT app or the network’s official website. Live sports broadcasts on TNT are also accessible through the HBO Max streaming platform via its sports add-on tier. For cord-cutters, several live TV streaming services carry TNT in their channel lineups. You can watch the broadcast live using platforms such as Sling TV, YouTube TV, Hulu + Live TV or DIRECTV STREAM. Verify that TNT is included in your specific subscription package prior to tip-off. Matchup Preview and Kalshi Markets Virginia brings a revamped offense leaning heavily on three-point attempts under Odom, led by freshman Thijs De Ridder. They face a tough test against Tennessee and projected lottery pick Nate Ament. The Volunteers lead the nation in offensive rebounding and are seeking their fourth straight Sweet 16 appearance. For fans looking to track the outcome of this game, Kalshi offers prediction markets where you can buy shares on either team advancing. Who Will Win? Tennessee vs Virginia Win Probabilities Data from Kalshi on March 21st. Based on the latest prediction markets on Kalshi, the crowd views this matchup as an exact tie. The implied probability of victory sits at 50.0% for the Tennessee Volunteers and 50.0% for the Virginia Cavaliers. Users are splitting their shares evenly between the two programs. The perfectly balanced percentages reflect expectations for a highly competitive game, positioning neither team as a favorite to advance. Creative Manager and Writer at Sportradar. Craig has previously worked as a 